## Quick Reference

Choose a branch ID from the table above:

```bash
neonctl branches list --project-id "{{PROJECT_ID}}" --output json
neonctl connection-string "<branchId>" --project-id "{{PROJECT_ID}}" \
  --database-name "{{DATABASE_NAME}}" --psql -- -c "SELECT 1;"
```

## Migration and Safety

Create a disposable branch with `neonctl branches create --project-id
"{{PROJECT_ID}}" --parent "<branchId>" --name "migration-check" --output json`.
Apply and verify migrations there before applying reviewed SQL through the
project's deployment process. Get explicit approval before production changes;
creating a branch does not promote schema changes.

Never run destructive SQL on production without explicit confirmation, or
`prisma migrate reset`, `prisma db push --force-reset`, or
`prisma db push --accept-data-loss` on shared branches. Confirm `DATABASE_URL`
targets the intended branch. Keep connection URLs out of logs.
